# Short lines in wiki pages

Never write long sentences in `docs/wiki/*.md`.

Do not pack a paragraph of facts into a single line.

Prefer short sentences. Do not turn every fact into a list.

Use a list only when the line would be very long, or the items are a real group such as steps or flags.

Use a number only when order matters. Otherwise `-` or `*`.

A list still needs a grouping line first.

```markdown
Query parameters:

- `transparent`
- `fontSize`
- `textColor`
```

Two or three short facts stay sentences:

```markdown
The window opens on **Home**. The local chat server starts with the app.
```

Tables and code fences may stay wide.
